1
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to me!

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,040
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:42,840
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

5
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:47,200
Wahhahahahahaha!

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me!

7
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,540
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

8
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:11,540
Look, the steel is burning too.

9
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

10
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,580
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

11
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:27,380
Once you understand,
follow me without a word.

12
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:43,440
Dance, Edo, the sabo!

13
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:49,660
Understood? Once you understand,
don't be late ever again.

14
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:54,180
Such a racket from the morning, geez.

15
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:02,680
Damn, today's the Yamanaka memorial, isn't it?
I forgot.

16
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:09,980
I'm pretty sure there's a park called Toyo Park around there,
you see.

17
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:12,820
It's near Toyo Elementary School, right?

18
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:19,900
When did he...?

19
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,940
That Ryotsu guy slipped
out on his own again!

20
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:26,160
But for him to disappear
without anyone noticing at all...

21
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,500
Ryo-chan really is a genius at escaping,
isn't he?

22
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:36,000
Damn, Number Two showed up right there!

23
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,640
So I'm stuck in debt again this month

24
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,460
Target H.2, is it?

25
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:47,880
Beach point passed.

26
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,780
I've been feeling eyes
on me for a while now.

27
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:54,940
Looks like the target has noticed us.

28
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:56,440
Right, capture him!

29
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:02,420
What?

30
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:20,340
W-what on earth is going on!

31
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,360
Ryotsu-kun

32
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,300
Chief!

33
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:30,100
Idiot!

34
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:33,320
What's the meaning of sneaking
out to go buy betting tickets!

35
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,460
Normally,
I'd give you a stern lecture and then

36
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:40,660
dock 80% of your salary,

37
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:42,560
80%!?

38
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,540
I really am reflecting on it.

39
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,160
I'll never do it again, I promise.

40
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:49,380
If you cut 80% of my pay,
I won't be able to eat.

41
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:52,260
Please, Chief, I'm begging you!

42
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,880
So then, Ryotsu-kun.

43
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,080
I have a special assignment for you.

44
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:10,080
Actually, we're going to hold a large-scale search drill, centered on 101 police stations and every police box,
using a new system that tracks a suspect through their PHS standby signal.

45
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:19,180
The scenario is that a violent criminal has escaped.
The search area covers the 23 wards of Tokyo and every area within the prefecture where the PHS signal reaches, and that fugitive...

46
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,240
You're going to do it, Ryotsu.

47
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,220
M-me?

48
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:27,220
Your quick getaway skills were more
than proven in the preliminary test.

49
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:29,660
So that's what that was all about.

50
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:30,960
What do you say, Ryotsu?

51
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:37,040
Your pay cut will be revoked, and if you manage
to escape completely, you'll receive a cash prize.

52
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,100
A cash prize?

53
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,900
So, Ryotsu,
will you take on this assignment?

54
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:46,240
Yes, sir! Officer Ryotsu gladly accepts!

55
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:48,720
Was it really all right
to say that to my senior?

56
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:51,560
Well, if they really show up,
it feels like he'd end up getting away...

57
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:54,640
Now then, from here on,

58
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:58,020
as planned, we will carry out
the large-scale search drill.

59
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:01,320
Everyone must work together as
one to carry out this assignment.

60
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,640
Also, the officers playing the criminals

61
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:07,460
have been told to act like
real violent criminals,

62
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,880
so don't hold back.

63
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,980
You should track them as
if they were real criminals.

64
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,380
There are three fugitives.

65
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:17,300
The goal is to arrest them within 48 hours.

66
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:20,500
That's the target.

67
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:31,760
Yes, understood. We start in three minutes.
Anyway, I just have to run, right?

68
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:39,100
Which route should we take? For now, JR.
We're starting. Everyone, turn on your PHS.

69
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,400
Got a signal.

70
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:49,300
All three are currently in front of the Tokyo
Street Hotel at the Tokyo Station Central Exit.

71
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:53,680
I'll catch all of them within an hour!

72
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,900
Then, on the Yamanote Line,

73
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:06,840
It's already here?
It hasn't even been a minute!

74
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,160
Ryotsu, what about the tickets?

75
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,060
Don't grab them on your own,
don't get caught.

76
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,020
Nakano Ward's...

77
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:15,320
Hey, we're the criminals, you know!

78
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:16,900
Well, yeah, but...

79
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:19,040
If we stick together, we'll stand out.
Let's split up.

80
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:21,660
I'll take the Chuo Line.

81
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:22,560
I'm on the inner loop.

82
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,720
I'm taking the outer loop.

83
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:27,520
Ryotsu won't make it in time.

84
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,980
Don't do anything reckless.

85
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,280
That's exactly how the suspect looks.

86
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,300
The suspects have split
up in three directions.

87
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,100
It looks like police officers
have entered Tokyo Station, but

88
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,820
We missed them by a hair!

89
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:48,340
But only this light keeps
flickering on and off.

90
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:49,140
Why?

91
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,040
They probably aren't inside the car.

92
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:54,040
They're probably outside the car,
near the pantograph.

93
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:54,540
What?

94
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:58,740
Damn it, is this a new-type train?

95
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,680
The windows won't open at all!

96
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:10,220
Right, they're already waiting
for us at the next station?

97
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,560
They're pretty good.

98
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,160
Alright, transfer!

99
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,820
Switching from one train
to another while running...

100
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:24,860
The one who'd pull a stunt like
that is probably the senior officer.

101
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:31,380
Just from that, you can tell? That's impressive.
One of the suspects is heading back toward Tokyo Station.

102
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:33,640
The officers at Tokyo
Station have already withdrawn.

103
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:43,740
We just received a report from the officer at Yurakucho Station that no suspects are on the train.
Understood, we're sending Ryo to Tokyo Station.

104
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:45,640
Hey, it's Tokyo Station

105
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:52,840
That's the situation. Count on your
cooperation with the investigation drill.

106
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:53,980
Understood.

107
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:58,320
Well, by now everyone should
be heading to Tokyo Station.

108
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,820
Here goes another one!

109
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:08,620
Sorry for startling you.

110
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:11,540
Please cooperate with
the investigation drill.

111
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,120
The suspect switched trains again.

112
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,760
What? That Ryotsu...

113
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:20,980
What should we do, Chief? Turn back again?

114
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:23,680
Yeah, let's watch them a while longer.

115
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:26,040
The suspect appears to be
in the middle of the car.

116
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:30,020
Officers, board from the front and
rear so the suspect doesn't notice you.

117
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:31,180
Team A, understood.

118
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,620
Team C, understood.

119
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,040
The rapid train is fast, isn't it?

120
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:43,780
What?

121
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,920
Damn! It won't stop until the next station,
so there's no way out!

122
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,920
We've spotted the suspect!
We're cornering them inside the car!

123
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,720
I shouldn't have gotten on the train!

124
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:55,600
From the front, too!

125
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,900
Sakonji Tatsunosuke won't be caught easily!

126
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:12,040
I'll teach you how hard it is to make an arrest,
the hard way!

127
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:14,720
How far do you think you'll get!

128
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:17,160
Run! Run!

129
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:18,100
Made the jump!

130
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:23,520
It looks like one of the suspects
has been cornered on the Chuo Line.

131
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:25,960
We've just received word that contact
with the suspect is in progress.

132
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:29,260
Alright! Good work!
Don't let him get away, no matter what!

133
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:35,120
The other one got off the train and is fleeing
through Akihabara's electronics district.

134
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:43,480
It's actually easier to escape in a crowd.

135
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:00,840
He's not here!

136
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,420
There he is!

137
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:27,900
Right.

138
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,360
Farewell, Akechi-kun, or whatever!

139
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,400
Damn it!

140
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:44,320
They even sent out a helicopter!

141
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:47,180
Next stop, Shimbashi, Shimbashi.

142
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,900
Ugh, there are so many
of them over here too!

143
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,240
They're definitely on this train.

144
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,520
Why?

145
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:35,660
We've cornered them this far,
so how can we not find them?

146
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:38,440
The helicopter reports
it can't spot them either.

147
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,340
The suspect is still moving along the line.

148
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,300
The helicopter has spotted the suspect.

149
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:58,280
They're making faces at us, apparently.

150
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:58,800
What?

151
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,760
The suspect has transferred
to the Yurikamome.

152
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:15,700
What?!

153
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:17,900
Now it's time for our trump card!

154
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,560
Special unit, move out!

155
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:25,560
Here we go!

156
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:33,300
Hold on!

157
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:50,660
The light has disappeared.

158
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:56,560
A report came in from the helicopter: the suspect vanished over Tokyo Bay,
near Harumi Wharf.

159
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,860
The special unit is
heading straight for Odaiba.

160
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,500
Damn it!

161
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:07,860
This is perfect. A leisurely
sky ride in an advertising blimp!

162
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,860
They're already here!

163
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:18,100
Somehow...

164
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:41,960
This is, well... unbearable!

165
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,080
Sorry.

166
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:48,120
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho!

167
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:51,540
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

168
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:13,720
Report from the police unit: the suspect
who was holding onto the blimp has vanished.

169
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,300
What?

170
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:18,680
The suspect appears to be
fleeing by car on the expressway.

171
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,180
What bastards!

172
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:34,440
The edge of the riverbank has no signal,
you know.

173
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:44,660
Anyway,
we've finally got everything cleaned up.

174
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:49,940
We can finally get down!

175
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:51,400
Yay!

176
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,660
Back to the same old loop again

177
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,120
Hello?

178
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:11,940
Yo, what's up?

179
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,640
The Volvo?

180
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:15,340
Where are you right now?

181
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,020
Lucky for us,
we landed in a truck's cargo bed.

182
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:20,760
If we'd gotten away on the expressway,
we wouldn't need this.

183
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,020
Nakagawa, you!

184
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,620
Why's that?

185
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,680
The expressway has an L-system
that's better than PHS!

186
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:30,060
And every exit is surrounded!

187
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,160
The police are good at that kind of thing!

188
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:33,960
W-what do we do?

189
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:37,300
Jump out right now and get down to
the ground by the emergency stairs!

190
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:39,300
A police car from behind!

191
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,000
No way, no, don't!

192
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:42,200
The Volvo, hey!

193
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:47,760
The Volvo got caught,
but what happened to Sakonji?

194
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:48,980
Durury!

195
00:15:49,980 --> 00:16:04,280
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

196
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:07,060
Let's go with the special love-hate version.
Victory!

197
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,340
Secured!

198
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,080
Damn it!

199
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:13,640
One suspect has been
arrested on the Chuo Line.

200
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:16,740
Sakonji got caught too

201
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:18,480
So that leaves just Ryotsu

202
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:20,220
It's Nakagawa and the others.

203
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:25,520
Those guys are dangerous.
They analyze my every move.

204
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:27,440
We've got a signal.

205
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,680
They're close by.

206
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:31,780
They seem to be within 100 to 500 meters.

207
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,340
It's gone.

208
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:43,740
Maybe he's inside this department store.

209
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,660
There isn't a single antenna inside.

210
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:48,500
If he's inside, we'll have no signal.

211
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:52,600
Besides, being up high is a good
way to keep track of police movements.

212
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:54,300
Alright, let's lock down the entrances.

213
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,560
And then contact headquarters.

214
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:55,920
Yes.

215
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:03,660
The suspect is in there.

216
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:06,340
There are antennas around
the department store.

217
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:08,180
The moment he comes out,
we should get a signal.

218
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:09,920
We'll arrest him when he comes out.

219
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:13,820
Even Ryotsu can't move around freely with a transmitter on him,
so he'll be easy to track.

220
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:17,940
There's a signal from another location.

221
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:18,940
That's impossible.

222
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:24,180
Inside, there was this.

223
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,220
How on earth did he get outside?

224
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:30,540
There was no signal at all!

225
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:33,660
He must have slipped through
a gap in the antenna coverage.

226
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,760
Cell phones cover a five-kilometer radius,

227
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:38,100
while PHS covers only 100 to 500 meters,

228
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,960
so the coverage area is narrow.

229
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:42,680
Every so often, very small gaps can form.

230
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:43,820
The suspect

231
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:46,180
found the gap that we can't cover,

232
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,800
and there's no other explanation.

233
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,720
Hah! He's like a cockroach!

234
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:54,720
One over there, and another over there too!

235
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,129
In that case,

236
00:17:57,179 --> 00:18:02,800
if he moves at this angle,
he'll be just barely outside the range,

237
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:14,340
Still haven't arrested the
last one after all this time!

238
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,080
Arrest him while he's sleeping at night!

239
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,540
We can't pinpoint his location.

240
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:21,280
Why?

241
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:26,600
He's probably sleeping on the roof of a
high-rise where the signal doesn't reach.

242
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:29,260
Then add more antennas.

243
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,540
Pack them in tight, so there are no gaps.

244
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:41,920
How many days has he been running now?

245
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:43,760
Let's see...

246
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:46,240
The ground's awfully noisy.

247
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:48,440
Is something happening?

248
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:53,320
All the patrol cars are
converging on this building!

249
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:54,180
What?

250
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:57,280
When did the antennas get here?

251
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:59,900
That's a dirty way of doing things!

252
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:04,760
Send out all the helicopters.

253
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:07,220
We'll catch him even if it
costs the police their honor.

254
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:20,320
They came at us with
a brute-force operation,

255
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,540
deploy the police dogs.

256
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:27,040
Make wanted posters too.

257
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,080
Isn't that against the rules?

258
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:31,620
We can't worry about rules at this point!

259
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:40,640
Damn, they're going all out.

260
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:43,020
At this rate,
we're treated like real criminals!

261
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,360
If they run an operation
on this large a scale,

262
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:59,900
What, they're not even cops?

263
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:04,100
You'd better fear me, Ushimatsu the terror!

264
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:06,660
So they're your buddies

265
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:11,720
Yeah, I'm the famous Ushimatsu, you know!

266
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:18,400
Dummies, dummies, I'm a police officer!

267
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:21,740
What a dirty trick!
You tricked me, you bastard!

268
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:23,940
It's useless, it won't come off.

269
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:26,920
We'll trace it back through you and pull
up the whole gang like a string of potatoes.

270
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:29,380
We're gonna arrest every last
member of the robbery gang, got it?

271
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:30,880
I'm warning you.

272
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:33,200
You can't make me spill anything, no way.

273
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:37,020
Among my crew,
I'm famous for being damn tight-lipped.

274
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:39,740
Don't count on it. Not with me.

275
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,300
Come on, come closer!

276
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:42,060
Hey!

277
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:42,640
Heyyy!

278
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,640
Robbery suspect!

279
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:46,620
That's right!

280
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,780
If I hand this guy over,
I'll get arrested too!

281
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:51,400
How do I...!

282
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:01,400
You're supposed to have vanished,
so why are you running away!

283
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,420
There are all sorts of reasons!

284
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:04,080
Ugh!

285
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:05,840
Antennas even out here!

286
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:10,380
We've got the suspect.
Looks like he's in the sewers.

287
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:12,220
Hey, arrest him.

288
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:52,080
Under the 20,000-volt power lines, the electromagnetic
waves are scrambled, so we shouldn't be detected.

289
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:55,040
Let's just go to the police station already,
the police!

290
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,140
I'll spill everything, you know.

291
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:57,760
No way!

292
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:09,040
Ryotsu-kun is completely surrounded.

293
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:10,760
Come out and resign yourself to it.

294
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:14,240
But it looks like someone is with him.

295
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:16,500
Ryotsu, give up already!

296
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:17,360
Damn it!

297
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:19,000
Whoa, they're the police!

298
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:19,940
Whoa!

299
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:23,220
Whoa!

300
00:22:23,220 --> 00:22:23,300
Whoa!

301
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:23,320
Whoa!

302
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:23,780
Ryotsu!

303
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:29,560
Come on, just let yourself
get caught already, come on!

304
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:30,880
Shut up!

305
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:34,140
Shut up!

306
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:34,700
Bababa!

307
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:36,400
Stop it, that's dangerous, Ryotsu!

308
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:39,360
Naaaaah!

309
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:40,660
Whoa!

310
00:22:42,300 --> 00:23:00,620
!

311
00:23:00,620 --> 00:23:03,620
Good work for now!
Contact headquarters and mobilize everyone!

312
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:06,280
We'll catch him in one fell
swoop with the Goto squad!

313
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:08,220
Everyone, start the search immediately!

314
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:08,820
Hah!

315
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:20,700
Look, Reiko, it's about this.

316
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:21,300
Yes.

317
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,200
Um... found it, found it.

318
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:25,040
Hey.

319
00:23:27,420 --> 00:23:28,620
Anyway!

320
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,120
S-senpai!

321
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:32,520
The real Ryo-chan?

322
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,171
That's right.

323
00:23:34,221 --> 00:23:37,640
Why aren't you looking for me?

324
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:40,780
The investigation training ended ages ago.

325
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:44,260
If it ended,
you should have told me right away.

326
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:49,000
Haunted every day by dreams of being chased,

327
00:23:49,050 --> 00:23:51,800
I've been running all over Tokyo.

328
00:23:51,860 --> 00:23:55,020
You idiot! Where else would you find an
idiot who keeps running for three months!

329
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:57,740
No salary for you! Your pay is docked!

330
00:23:58,100 --> 00:24:00,280
W-what... that's...

331
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:02,560
Forget it...

332
00:24:37,340 --> 00:24:45,220
I walked only on the black
tiles of the Edo street.

333
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:53,620
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

334
00:24:54,580 --> 00:25:00,920
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties whose eyebrows wobble.

335
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:06,540
Go on, turn that corner over there.

336
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:11,740
You can meet everyone, everyone!

337
00:25:12,320 --> 00:25:19,680
Over there, there's a wall.
Well, surely there's a wall.

338
00:25:20,940 --> 00:25:24,940
Everybody come on over to our town!

339
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:26,480
Thank you.

340
00:25:29,260 --> 00:25:31,600
Volvo, what happened? Whose dog is that?

341
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:35,060
This is Bobby,
the Doberman I'm looking after for Jodie.

342
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:38,420
Don't go getting all mushy just
because the dog was named after you.

343
00:25:38,900 --> 00:25:41,540
But your apartment doesn't allow pets,
does it?

344
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,740
What on earth are you planning to do?

345
00:25:44,180 --> 00:25:46,640
Next time, I'll teach you how to keep a pet.

346
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:47,740
Take care.

347
00:25:48,780 --> 00:25:50,940
Over there is Kameari.

348
00:25:51,980 --> 00:25:54,600
Mar-kid Kameari.

349
00:25:57,480 --> 00:25:59,280
To our town!

350
00:26:00,220 --> 00:26:00,880
Thank you!

